index 4479b53..5e5a4a0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,46 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkey UI integration
+
+Sign-in and sign-up support browser WebAuthn alongside passwords. Account security is at
+`/devtools-times/account/settings` (also linked from the header and footer). The UI supports
+adding, renaming, removing, and reauthenticating with passkeys, with password reauthentication
+as an alternative. HTTPS or localhost and a WebAuthn-capable browser are required.
+
+The authentication service is external to this repository. Set `PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL` at build
+time to override the existing Cloud Functions API URL. **The service must implement the
+following contract before passkey flows can succeed.** No credentials or successful
+verifications are simulated locally.
+
+| Endpoint | Request | Response |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `POST /login`, `POST /register` | `{ username, password }` | `{ token? }` or authenticated cookie |
+| `GET /passkeys` | Authenticated session | `{ passkeys: [{ id, name, createdAt, lastUsedAt?, deviceType? }] }` |
+| `POST /passkeys/register/options` | `{ username? , name?, verificationToken? }` | `{ options, challengeId }` |
+| `POST /passkeys/authenticate/options` | `{ username? }` | `{ options, challengeId }` |
+| `POST /passkeys/reauthenticate/options` | Authenticated session | `{ options, challengeId }` |
+| `POST /passkeys/{register,authenticate}/verify` | `{ credential, challengeId, username?, name?, verificationToken? }` | `{ token? }` or authenticated cookie |
+| `POST /passkeys/reauthenticate/verify` | `{ credential, challengeId }` | `{ verificationToken }` |
+| `POST /reauthenticate` | `{ password }` | `{ verificationToken }` |
+| `PATCH /passkeys/:id` | `{ name, verificationToken }` | Successful JSON response |
+| `DELETE /passkeys/:id` | `{ verificationToken }` | Successful response |
+| `POST /logout` | Authenticated session | Successful response; invalidate cookie and token |
+
+Options use base64url strings for binary WebAuthn fields. The client converts them to
+ArrayBuffers and serializes authenticator responses back to base64url. The API must issue
+short-lived, single-use challenges; verify signatures, origins, RP IDs, user verification,
+and account ownership; and enforce reauthentication for all management actions. Registration
+for a new username must create its account only after verification. Use discoverable
+credentials (`residentKey: 'required'`) and require user verification for passkeys. Removing
+the last sign-in method must be rejected by the service.
+
+Bearer tokens returned by the existing API are kept in sessionStorage and sent in the
+Authorization header. Cookie sessions are sent using `credentials: 'include'`; cross-origin
+hosting requires the service's CORS and cookie policies to permit the configured app origin.
+Password registration without a returned token redirects to sign-in. Reauthentication tokens
+are used only for the requested action. API failures remain visible with retry or sign-in
+options; failed verification never unlocks a management action.
+
+WebAuthn reference: [W3C Web Authentication](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/).
